WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.450
A busy street rushes past you.

2
00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:06.880
Shop signs, faces,
buses, flashing colours.

3
00:00:06.930 --> 00:00:10.320
Replay it, and your eyes
caught almost all of it.

4
00:00:10.370 --> 00:00:13.550
But a minute later, a
friend asks what you saw.

5
00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:16.320
You can describe just a handful of things.

6
00:00:16.370 --> 00:00:19.190
So out of everything
that reached your eyes,

7
00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:22.470
what decided which few things stayed?

8
00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:25.480
In this mission, you'll
meet the multi-store model,

9
00:00:25.530 --> 00:00:28.740
which says memory is
made of separate stores.

10
00:00:28.790 --> 00:00:31.470
The first store holds a very large amount.

11
00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:34.610
But for sights, it lasts under a second.

12
00:00:34.660 --> 00:00:38.680
Short-term memory is tiny by
comparison: about 7 items,

13
00:00:38.730 --> 00:00:40.440
plus or minus 2.

14
00:00:40.490 --> 00:00:44.590
Your mission: find out what
decides which few things you keep.
